{
 "about": "How well the quoted error bars of the paper's higher-order model cover the truth with the growth-tied linear-bias prior, against the same model on the correlated (pessimistic) prior, at every cut. Fit: model B + tilts; growth-tied: every bin of a DESI group follows B_g/D(zbar_i), one amplitude per group, no tilt and no residual; correlated prior: the pessimistic prior (L = 0.05, 3% per group). Truths: the known drifts (a conserved population, the r < 19.5 flux limit in BGS) plus a residual drawn from the pessimistic prior. eta = sqrt(<chi2>/n_dof), averaged exactly over the truths and the data noise (n_dof = 2 for (w0, wa), 1 for Omega_m or A_s; 1 = honest error bars); coverage: the probability that the truth falls inside the fit's 68.3% region. Written by EXAMPLE_EVALUATE_FISHER_MODEL_B.ipynb (section 9) at the final derivative tier.",
